  message: "CHECK 2026-10-05 (losod run, owner sequence \"check hular after losod/faful\"). ALREADY MET ON origin/dev, and NOT by WI-losod / WI-faful.\n\nRe-ran this item's own repro (the two fixtures from ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gujoh_09242026/fx3/, copied to ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/losod/fx/hular_with_req and hular_with_direct) with hypergumbo verify-claims, claim host_secret -> network, --format json:\n- origin/dev tree (git archive of 222c1c3ded): both fixtures read urlopen ddg / confirmed.\n- stage-8b base c1dd831558: both ddg / confirmed.\n- losod branch (11a10f98b0..a9e3a869f4): both ddg / confirmed (unchanged).\nControl: the plain-call shape (return urlopen(url, data=secret.encode())) reads ddg / confirmed in all three trees.\n\nThe acceptance condition (\"both fixtures above read ddg / confirmed at urlopen\") is met. Mechanism: a53ff18377 (2026-09-26, WI-simiv), two days after this item was filed: the with header is recorded as context_manager_enter with ast_node_type set to the with_clause, so populate_def_use_for_cfg runs py_def_use's new with_clause handler on it (as-targets defined, value expressions used), and the clause is no longer uncovered code. Not the same statement-model gap as WI-losod/WI-faful, so nothing changed for it on the losod branch. Evidence files: losod/before.txt, losod/hular_odev.txt, losod/after.txt. Status left to the owner."  # fe60
